## ❗ Issues Faced

While running the code, we encountered the following error:

```
KeyboardInterrupt
```

### 🔍 Analysis of the Issue

* The error occurred during library import (NumPy / Transformers)
* The process was taking too long and was manually interrupted
* This indicates heavy computation or memory overload

---

## ⚠️ Hardware Limitations

The main issue was not with the code, but with system limitations.

### 🖥️ System Configuration:

* 16GB RAM
* 256GB SSD
* No high-end GPU

### 📊 Model Requirements (Gemma 31B):

| Format | Approx Memory Needed |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| FP32   | ~120 GB              |
| FP16   | ~60 GB               |
| 8-bit  | ~30 GB               |
| 4-bit  | ~15–20 GB            |

### 🚫 Conclusion:

* The model is too large to run on a standard laptop
* Even downloading the model (~4GB+ initial files, full much larger) is resource-intensive
* The system may freeze, slow down, or crash

---

## 🧠 Key Learnings

* Not all LLMs can run locally
* Model size directly impacts hardware requirements
* Multimodal models (image + text) are heavier than text-only models
* Proper environment setup (Python version, virtual env) is important
* Interrupting long processes can cause `KeyboardInterrupt` errors

